<title>SINGAPORE: Singapore weekly residues and distillates down.</title>
<headline>Singapore weekly residues and distillates down.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-11-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Singapore weekly residue stocks fell by 507,000 barrels in the week ended November 13 to 11.107 million barrels, Singapore's Trade Development Board (TDB) said.</p>
<p>They include HSFO, LSFO, LSWR and the straight-run atmospheric residue, but exclude bitumen.</p>
<p>Middle-distillate stocks also fell by 322,000 barrels to 9.018 million barrels. Middle distillates comprise jet, kerosene and gas oil.</p>
<p>Light distillate stocks slipped by 414,000 barrels to 5.379 million barrels. They comprise gasoline, reformate and naphtha.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65-870-3082)</p>
